    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d109-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0140" n="66" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg66"/>

                <head>[Enclosure.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Department, Second
                                Agency,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Memphis, Tennessee,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-12-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 29, 1864,</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>W. E. Scanlan, a British subject, is hereby permitted to remove his crop of
                    cotton, produced during the year 1864, from Scanlan’s landing, eighteen miles
                    below Memphis, to Memphis to be stored, and reported at this office for further
                    action.</p>
                <p>This is a case in which I am acting on special instructions from the Secretary of
                    the Treasury, and I recommend the military authorities to give such passes as
                    may be necessary in the case.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W. ORME, <hi rendition="#italic">Supervising Special
                        Agent.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
